looning  works  as follows: The host operator requests a guest to
return some amount of memory to the host (via e.g.  Qemu  monitor
balloon  command).   The  hypervisor sends the request via VirtIO
memory ballooning device.  The guest driver  requests  allocation
of that amount of physical memory from the memory management sys‐
tem.   The  device tells the hypervisor the guest physical memory
address of the allocated memory via VirtIO memory ballooning  de‐
vice.  The sysctl node shows the requested number of memory pages
to  return  to  the  hypervisor, while shows the actual number of
memory pages that are already returned to  the  hypervisor.   The
